This fixture is DISTRIBUTION-ONLY. It must never be copied to a consumer.

Its subject is scripts/render-path-mapping.sh, this repository's own program. install.sh's
copy loop reads core/scripts/ and core/, never scripts/, so the renderer ships nowhere: on a
consumer this fixture's resolver would find no scripts/render-path-mapping.sh in either
layout and exit 2 before any arm ran. Its controlA and controlE arms then run `--check`
against the real repo root, which on a consumer tree is a root that has no renderer to run.

The consumer DOES hold the renderer's source and target -- preclassify.sh and SKILL.md land
under .claude/skills/ai-dlc-update/ -- which is exactly why this marker is easy to get wrong
in the shipping direction. The subject is the RENDERER, not what it reads, and the renderer
is not there.

A fixture whose subject is absent cannot fail, and a unit that cannot fail scores as a pass
in the consumer's own suite verdict.

It is also a MUTATION BATTERY: it builds ten throwaway repos per run and edits copies of
map_consumer()'s own source and of the rendered region in SKILL.md.
